<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<templates xml:space="preserve">

    <!-- Two entries in the till's burger menu that a cashier should not be
         offered.

         "Backend" was not ungated: pos_hr already sets t-if="showBackend",
         which is true when the cashier IS the signed-in user, and true for
         everyone when employee login is switched off. That is a test of
         SESSION OWNERSHIP, not of permission, which is why the parent
         company's register (employee login off) showed it to anyone standing
         at it.

         So the two conditions are ANDed rather than swapped: core still
         decides whether the door exists for this session, and this decides
         whether the person is senior enough to walk through it. Replacing
         showBackend outright would have thrown away the module_pos_hr case
         core is handling.

         Relabelled to match the lock screen too, because one place calling
         it "Backend" and another "Admin Panel / Control Center" is how a
         shop ends up with two names for one door.

         "Create Product" is already gated on real product create rights, so
         a cashier who can see it genuinely holds them, so the fix there is the
         account rather than the menu. It is narrowed to managers as well so the
         till agrees with how this shop is actually run: prices and new lines
         are set in the office, where there is a full form, a cost, a brand
         and a category, rather than mid-queue.

         _role is core's own signal (pos_hr/hr_employee.py sets manager /
         cashier / minimal, and res_users.py the same for a non-employee
         login), which is what the neighbouring Install App and Cash In/Out
         entries already test. -->
    <t t-name="pos_retail.NavbarManagerOnly" t-inherit="point_of_sale.Navbar"
       t-inherit-mode="extension">
        <!-- Replaced whole rather than patched: the label is the element's
             own text, and appending to it would read "Backend Admin Panel /
             Control Center". -->
        <xpath expr="//DropdownItem[@onSelected='() => pos.closePos()']" position="replace">
            <DropdownItem t-if="showBackend and this.pos.cashier._role == 'manager'"
                          onSelected="() => pos.closePos()">
                Admin Panel / Control Center
            </DropdownItem>
        </xpath>
        <xpath expr="//DropdownItem[@t-if='showCreateProductButton']" position="attributes">
            <attribute name="t-if">showCreateProductButton and this.pos.cashier._role == 'manager'</attribute>
        </xpath>
    </t>

</templates>
